  "body": "Adds the `delete_tool` MCP tool (#734; `edit_tool` already shipped in #1062).\n\nWhat changed\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/tool_delete.rs`: runs the app's undoable `DeleteTool` through `env.history.execute`, one undo step (undo restores number, body, cutter).\n- Refused by tool name, nothing changed: unknown name, a non-tool entity, and a tool any operation still uses (names the first operation; points at `set_tool`). The refusal lives in the MCP layer, not in `DeleteTool::new`, because the GUI and existing tests delete in-use tools; changing the command is a separate decision.\n- Registered beside `edit_tool` in `mcp/tools.rs`; row added to `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`; `PROCESS_VERSION` 50 -> 51 (settle at merge).\n\nPinning tests (`crates/app/tests/mcp_delete_tool.rs`)\n- `delete_tool_removes_it_and_undo_redo_walk_it`\n- `delete_tool_refuses_a_tool_an_operation_uses`\n- `delete_tool_refuses_an_unknown_name_and_a_non_tool`\nMutation-checked: disabling the in-use check fails the second; making the delete a no-op fails the first; dropping the name from the unknown-tool message fails the third.\n\nGates: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (app suites, 66 s); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Not exercised: GUI, UI suites.\n\nChangelog: `delete_tool` MCP tool: delete a document tool (undoable), refusing an unknown or in-use tool by name (#734)\nEffort: medium (no escalation)\nFork synced at upstream main b45f71a0.\n\nFixes #734\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
